WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.894
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition Twenty-Nine.

2
00:00:03.894 --> 00:00:16.479
A transversal cutting parallel lines makes the alternate interior angles equal, the exterior angle equal to the opposite interior angle, and the interior angles on the same side supplementary.

3
00:00:16.479 --> 00:00:21.198
Let segment E F fall on parallel segments A B and C D at points G and H.

4
00:00:21.198 --> 00:00:32.210
We prove that alternate angles A G H and G H D are equal, exterior angle E G B equals interior angle G H D, and interior angles B G H and G H D sum to two right angles.

5
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:37.140
Suppose angle A G H is not equal to angle G H D, and let angle A G H be greater.

6
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:43.454
Adding angle B G H to each, the sum of angles A G H and B G H is greater than the sum of angles B G H and G H D.

7
00:00:43.454 --> 00:00:51.403
By Proposition Thirteen, adjacent angles A G H and B G H equal two right angles, so angles B G H and G H D sum to less than two right angles.

8
00:00:51.403 --> 00:01:00.254
By Postulate Five, lines extended from interior angles summing to less than two right angles must meet, contradicting that segments A B and C D are parallel.

9
00:01:00.254 --> 00:01:02.960
Thus alternate angles A G H and G H D are equal.

10
00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:08.839
Again, by Proposition Fifteen, vertical angles A G H and E G B are equal.

11
00:01:08.839 --> 00:01:14.523
By Common Notion One, exterior angle E G B also equals interior angle G H D.

12
00:01:14.523 --> 00:01:23.797
Adding angle B G H to each by Common Notion Two, the sum of angles E G B and B G H equals the sum of angles B G H and G H D.

13
00:01:23.797 --> 00:01:36.660
Since adjacent angles E G B and B G H equal two right angles by Proposition Thirteen, interior angles B G H and G H D also equal two right angles, as was required to prove.
